examples.solution_text:
(a) Draw an open circle at $-1$ because the boundary is excluded. Draw the arrow left towards smaller values.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,color=black]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-4.5,0)--(4.5,0);
\foreach \v in {-4,...,4} {\draw (\v,0.1)--(\v,-0.1);\path (\v,-0.15) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\draw[very thick,-{Stealth}] (-1,0)--(-4.35,0);
\draw[fill=white] (-1,0) circle (2.4pt);
\path (4.6,0) node[right,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) Draw a closed circle at $2$ because the boundary is included. Draw the arrow right towards larger values.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,color=black]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-4.5,0)--(4.5,0);
\foreach \v in {-4,...,4} {\draw (\v,0.1)--(\v,-0.1);\path (\v,-0.15) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\draw[very thick,-{Stealth}] (2,0)--(4.35,0);
\fill (2,0) circle (2.4pt);
\path (4.6,0) node[right,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

