examples.solution_text:
$0\le x$ means $x\ge0$. Include $0$ and draw the arrow right.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,color=black]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-4.5,0)--(4.5,0);
\foreach \v in {-4,...,4} {\draw (\v,0.1)--(\v,-0.1);\path (\v,-0.15) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\draw[very thick,-{Stealth}] (0,0)--(4.35,0);
\fill (0,0) circle (2.4pt);
\path (4.6,0) node[right,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$x\le0$ includes $0$ and the values to its left.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,color=black]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-4.5,0)--(4.5,0);
\foreach \v in {-4,...,4} {\draw (\v,0.1)--(\v,-0.1);\path (\v,-0.15) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\draw[very thick,-{Stealth}] (0,0)--(-4.35,0);
\fill (0,0) circle (2.4pt);
\path (4.6,0) node[right,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The first includes positive numbers; the second includes negative numbers. Both include $0$.

Draw a closed circle at $-1$ and an open circle at $4$. Join them to show all values between the boundaries.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,color=black]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.5,0)--(5.5,0);
\foreach \v in {-2,...,5} {\draw (\v,0.1)--(\v,-0.1);\path (\v,-0.15) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\draw[very thick] (-1,0)--(4,0);
\fill (-1,0) circle (2.4pt);
\draw[fill=white] (4,0) circle (2.4pt);
\path (5.6,0) node[right,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

